Thanks for the feedback!  I think that improved our ALSA driver
significantly (attached!)

On Tue, Oct 13, 2009 at 12:03 AM, Clemens Ladisch <clemens@ladisch.de> wrot=
e:
> Sam Lantinga wrote:
>> I'm attaching the latest versions of the SDL audio files, and I'd
>> really appreciate it if you take a look and sanity check our code.
>
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 device =3D SDL_getenv("AUDIODEV"); =A0 =A0 =A0 =A0/* Is ther=
e a standard variable name? */
>
> ALSA's devices look at certain environment variables; you are supposed
> to use names like "default" or "surround51" to get that default
> configuration.
>
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 if (channels =3D=3D 6) device =3D "surround51";
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 else if (channels =3D=3D 4) device =3D "surround40";
>
> The devices do not have automatic sample format/rate conversion; you
> might want to use "plug:surround.." instead.
>
>> /* This function waits until it is possible to write a full sound buffer=
 */
>> static void ALSA_WaitAudio(_THIS)
>
> This function doesn't actually wait ...
>
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 if ( status =3D=3D -EAGAIN ) {
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 =A0 =A0 =A0 =A0 SDL_Delay(1);
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 =A0 =A0 =A0 =A0 continue;
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 }
>
> Not necessary in blocking mode.
>
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 rate =3D spec->freq;
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 status =3D SDL_NAME(snd_pcm_hw_params_set_rate_near)(pcm_han=
dle, hwparams, &rate, NULL);
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 spec->freq =3D rate;
>
> The returned rate could be wildly different, but I guess SDL correctly
> handles the new value in spec->freq.
>
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 /* Set the buffer size, in samples */
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 frames =3D spec->samples;
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 status =3D SDL_NAME(snd_pcm_hw_params_set_period_size_near)(=
pcm_handle, hwparams, &frames, NULL);
>
> This does _not_ set the buffer size.
>
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 periods =3D 2;
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 SDL_NAME(snd_pcm_hw_params_set_periods_near)(pcm_handle, hwp=
arams, &periods, NULL);
>
> A bigger number of periods would make the writing of audio data less
> bursty.
>
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 status =3D SDL_NAME(snd_pcm_sw_params_set_start_threshold)(p=
cm_handle, swparams, 0);
>
> Zero doesn't really make sense; the default value 1 would be OK.
>
>> =A0 =A0 =A0 status =3D SDL_NAME(snd_pcm_sw_params_set_avail_min)(pcm_han=
dle, swparams, frames);
>
> The default value is the period size anyway, so you can remove this.
> (If you change the buffer size code above to use _set_buffer_size_near,
> this call would be wrong.)
>
>
> Best regards,
> Clemens
>



